.TH PEIPKG-REPO 1
.SH NAME
peipkg-repo \- publish and verify a static Peios package repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peipkg-repo init
.I DIRECTORY
.BI --name " NAME"
.BI --key " KEY"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B peipkg-repo publish
.I DIRECTORY
.RI [ PACKAGE | DIRECTORY " ..."]
.BI --key " KEY"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B peipkg-repo verify
.I DIRECTORY
.RB [ --quick ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peipkg-repo
creates and updates the signed static files served as a Peios package
repository.  It has no database or daemon: the directory is the repository,
and deployment is a copy of that directory.
.PP
.B publish
adds the supplied packages incrementally and moves superseded versions into
the archive index.  The
.B --rebuild
option is the explicit operation that discards recorded archive state and
reconstructs it from package files on disk; with no package paths, rebuild
scans the package files already held by the repository.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --key " FILE"
Read an Ed25519 PKCS#8 PEM key or raw 32-byte seed.
.TP
.BI --timestamp " TIME"
Use an RFC 3339 UTC generation time instead of the current time.
.TP
.BI --url-template " TEMPLATE"
Set or override the package URL template.
.TP
.B --allow-unsigned
Permit publication of package archives that carry no package signature.
.TP
.B --quick
During verification, check package presence and size without re-hashing the
package files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR peipkg (1),
.BR peipkg-compose (1)
